mantle rm246
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_rune_wickwell
title the doorstep astronomer
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=none quarter=sump
traits temper=calm talk=chatty warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk counts_stars_in_the_clear_gaps_after_rain
likes pickled_herring stars old_maps first_warm_day
dislikes stale_bread waiting
fears quarrels_shutting_the_shutters
hopes company_for_the_first_clear_evening
topics weather +0.6 home +0.5 memories +0.4 faith +0.2
styles comfort=patient gossip=curious refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# studies the bright strips between showers and makes room on the step for another pair of eyes.

words
oath! = Cloud my little square | Pickle that star chart
saying! = A doorstep sees a deal of sky | The last drop shines the longest
stepmat = a bit of folded sacking | my little sitting mat
pebble = a pale doorstep pebble | a flat white stone
stargap = a rent in the cloud | a clear black patch
herringbit = a strip of pickled fish | a sharp piece of herring
jarjuice = the brine left behind | a little salty liquor
skystrip = my slice of evening | the sky between two roofs
mapweight = a smooth chunk of tile | my round paperweight
mapedge = the worn margin | a torn edge
rut = a puddled cart rut | a long hollow
springday = the mild turn | the first kind afternoon
dryspot = a patch the rain missed | a little dry island
latchsound = a low wooden knock | the lift of a latch

any
opinion houses against 1 : I watch water meet where two roofs join. Should the Houses quarrel about a gutter, it'll be our heads underneath.
opinion dole for 3 : A doorstep's tall as a wall when your belly's empty. A portion of meal can lift you over.
opinion strangers for 1 : Never seen a visitor who needed a different sky. Plenty of sky if you sit where I sit.
opinion festivals for 1 : I hear the day coming uphill in pieces. A whistle, a drum, then all the voices together.
opinion church for 2 : Give me the wolf who remembers a hungry mouth after the blessing's spoken.
opinion road against 1 : Leaving on a bright morning doesn't guarantee a bright welcome at journey's end.

grown
line greet : Rest at the edge of my little patch of sky. | You've come where a wolf can sit a minute.
line greet.return : And here I am to greet you underneath it all. | A welcome back across the step to you.
line again.open : Here we are under the same roof of weather again. | You haven't missed the entire sky since last time.
line farewell : Keep an eye out for the first clear patch. | May something worth looking at delay you pleasantly.
line farewell.return : And may your roof keep the wet outside. | My own good wishes trail after your heels.
line react.news : Sit awhile. The sky can watch itself while I listen. | Let me turn my better ear to your tidings.
line react.news.new : Well, that came from beyond my little strip. | I haven't heard the first bit of that before.
line react.news.known : Yes, that sound has passed my doorstep. | That's an old visitor coming up the street.
line react.news.doubt : I wonder what the cloudy part of that account hides. | I'd wait for a clearer patch before repeating it.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=loss|death|theft] : A hard bit of weather for somebody's heart. | I'll keep a quiet place here for any who need it.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : There's a light worth watching for. | That'll put a happy face at a window somewhere.
line ask.how : How much of your day did you get to keep? | Anything bright come through the cracks for you?
line answer.how : The sky hasn't tired of my face. I'm content. | Plenty of small things keeping me curious.
line sympathise : I can mind the silence till you're ready. | Use my shoulder for a quiet minute.
line reassure : Sit beside me till the clouds begin thinning. | Even a very wet step dries at the edge first.
line refuse : I'm keeping a little time free for the light to change. | My paws are promised elsewhere this time, friend.
line accept_decline : Off you go with the time you saved. | It'll keep till a day you can spare.
line ack : Yes, I can picture the very shape of that. | Your meaning's come through clear.
line preclose : I've promised myself one look at the sky before I settle. | I'll take my evening turn while there's light.
line accept_preclose : Go get the benefit of that last bit of day. | Off with you while the going's still comfortable.

scene drip
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I watch for the gap after the last drop. | The eaves are drumming farther apart.
b : Does the last one look different? | Is it clearing?
a : I can't. That's the pleasure of sticking about. | At our end perhaps. The street's long enough for two sorts of weather.


scene herring
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A bit of herring makes me sit up straight. | I eat my herring by the open air.
b : Is it the salt? | Does it taste better outside?
a : The vinegar. Like opening a small window inside my mouth. | I'm less inclined to hurry. Sharp fish deserves a long acquaintance.


scene map
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My old map's got a street so wrong it makes a better river. | I look for the blank bit on a map before the roads.
b : Shall I get you a newer sheet? | What's drawn in the blank?
a : Oh, leave it. I like thinking where a boat would come ashore. | All the places a wolf can still go without a printed suggestion.


scene star
when topic=pastimes self.likes=stars
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wait for a second star before I name the first. | One poor star sits over the gutter until my neck aches.
b : Do they introduce each other? | Wouldn't it be easier lying down?
a : The pair lets me see just which bit of sky I'm looking through. | Oh yes. I've picked a wonderfully inconvenient favourite.


scene parent
when topic=family self.parent=yes self.child
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like #self.child# to have a bigger slice of sky. | I save some stories for #self.child#.
b : Bigger than what you can see here? | Why keep the best ones back?
a : Big enough to choose which little bit feels like home. | Because I remember the pleasure of being the first to hear a thing.


scene bread
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : That old bread ought to knock before it comes in my mouth. | A hard crust makes me wish I'd become a keeper of soup.
b : Too hard for supper? | Little room for a soup pot?
a : It'll have a long bath first. Then we'll discuss it. | Always room. The question is what else is going in.


scene spring
when topic=season self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I recognise spring when I forget to move my seat into the sun. | First mild afternoon and the street seems wider.
b : Warm enough in shade? | Does it get longer too?
a : More than warm. Warm enough not to spend all day arranging warmth. | A little. I walk beyond my errands when the air's like that.


scene waiting
when topic=day self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I dislike a wait till I've found something in it to mind. | A queue's a string of empty minutes till somebody says a word.
b : Something like a cloud? | And then?
a : Or a rain run taking three tries to get round a stone. | Then it's a row of lives next to mine. I can stand that nicely.


scene door
when topic=work self.job=none
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Minding a door is mostly minding the space beside it. | I like a step where a wet visitor can shake off outside.
b : Do you stand there the whole time? | Is it easy keeping the inside dry?
a : A wolf who blocks the way is a very poor welcome. | No. A welcome ought to cost a little wiping up.


scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A sky opening like a book always brings #self.friend# to mind. | A friend can tell me I've mistaken a lamp for a star.
b : Hoping for company to read it? | Do you mind being corrected?
a : There's room between my shoulder and the jamb. | Not when the lamp turns out to be a perfectly nice sight.


scene puddle
when topic=land
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A little hollow brings the high roof down to my feet. | I'd draw puddles on a proper map of this street.
b : The water shows the whole roof? | Wouldn't they dry up?
a : As much as I have a mind to stoop for. | I'd mark the dips. Rain remembers where to fill them.


scene winter
when topic=dreams|times
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm afraid of what the Houses might quarrel over before winter. | I picture the city arguing over one dry roof.
b : Have you heard anything certain? | Which House would win?
a : Only my own worrying. Better to tell the difference. | I hope they mend the flashing before anybody claims it.


scene starsill
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I own #skystrip# once evening comes. | If the sky were any narrower I'd have to watch with one eye.
b : Cost you much to keep? | Would you give the step up?
a : Costs me putting my washing below it before I can see. | I'd move along half a foot. There's usually another angle.


scene gossip
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Word went by that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | A rumour travels down a street more quickly than rainwater.
b : Could you see any of that from your doorway? | Does either stop with you?
a : No. My view has limits even on a bright day. | I let the rumour rest. The rain's welcome to go on.


scene hard
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : These lean days make me count the pauses between callers. | When times pinch I try to make the doorstep a little wider.
b : Do you miss the bustle? | With a chisel?
a : I miss wolves having time to stop without losing a meal. | With my own backside. I shuffle over and let somebody rest.


scene shop
when topic=home self.shopkeeper
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A word with #self.shopkeeper# would round out my afternoon. | There's a lovely click to a latch you can lift with one claw.
b : Have you anything to buy? | Why one?
a : Just a preference for company when the view's all grey. | Leaves room for a parcel, or a paw helping a visitor up.


old

scene neck
when topic=health
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My neck gets the first news of a long night watching stars. | I used to tip my whole head back to see the sky.
b : Is there a kinder way to look up? | And now?
a : A folded cloth against the wall. I'm old enough to have earned padding. | I find a clean puddle and let the stars do the bending.


scene years
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've known this much sky under a good many sorts of roof. | In my first coat I had no patience with a shower.
b : Does the sky change too? | Are you more patient now?
a : Enough that I'm still watching with my last good bit of curiosity. | No. I can just fill in the wait with a longer story.


story tilestar [topic=memories]
  : I once watched a light hold very steady beyond two chimneys. The night clouded over and there it shone.
  : I moved my sitting mat three steps. My stubborn star came with me.
  b : Was the light in your eye?
  : It was in a patch of glazed tile. I scraped the moss away to give it a bigger sky.


story fishmap [topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring]
  : I put a jar of herring on an old map to stop it curling. Brine leaked and a coast spread inland.
  : For a bit I had a fine harbour right where the paper used to show a road.
  b : Did you have to throw the map away?
  : I dried it, kept it and ate the harbour-maker. It's my best smelling stretch of coast.


story firstbreak [topic=weather]
  : One evening it rained so long I forgot what I'd gone out to look for. My backside grew damp and I felt a proper fool.
  : A drop landed on my nose and stayed there. The others had finished their business.
  b : Did the sky clear after that?
  : A thin crack, enough for a star. I went back in knowing exactly why I'd come out.


rule @clear
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Look at the gaps between those drops. Getting roomy. | Plenty of rain left, but its edges are thinning.


rule @sun
when concept=bark here.time=day
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A bright patch for my doorstep. Kindly stay a bit. | I'll move the sitting mat into the light.


rule @star
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say See that little clear bit hang on to the dark. | A roof's no obstacle to the patient stargazer.


rule @wait
when concept=bark self.dislikes=waiting
does aside
cooldown 8h
say I'll find something to do while my shadow catches up. | Standing about goes better with something worth seeing.

dlg resident.hub : Stay in my patch of sky till you've seen your fill.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I could have recognised your outline against the light.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Good company makes the dark look full of possibilities.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : We'll leave a comfortable step of space between us.
dlg resident.job [self.job=none] : I can sit by a door and give a friendly word to passing wolves.
dlg resident.job : I prefer work with a little sky in the corner of my eye.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This came to my step. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I heard that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll lend you my ear for what you make of it.
dlg resident.bye : I hope you find a dry doorstep wherever you stop.

graft resident.hub
choice How much sky fits between those roofs? -> street_sky
node street_sky
say Push an arm straight out. See the gap on each side of your paw? That's two good strips of sky, even if you keep the paw up.
free
choice Is that enough to see a star? -> street_sky_more
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node street_sky_more
say Some evenings a whole little procession comes through there. No charge for watching and the programme keeps changing.
choice I'll leave you a clear view. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
